==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|l|u}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*loodak}}, from {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*loŋe-||to throw, push away}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|luo|da|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|uodɑ|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/ˈluɔdɑ(ʔ)/}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{lb|fi|transitive}} To [[create]].
#: ''Alussa Jumala '''loi''' taivaan ja maan.''
#:: ''In the beginning God '''created''' the heaven and the earth.'' (Gen. 1:1)
# {{lb|fi|transitive}} ''luoda [[lumi|lunta]]'': To [[shovel]] [[snow]].
# {{lb|fi|transitive}} To [[shed]].
#: ''Lamppu '''luo''' sinistä valoa.''
#:: The lamp '''sheds''' a blue light.
# To [[exuviate]], [[slough]], [[molt]] (to shed or cast off a covering, especially a skin); used always with an object that reveals what is being exuviated.
#: ''Käärme alkoi '''luoda nahkaansa'''.''
#:: The snake began to '''exuviate''' its '''old skin'''.
#: ''Kun hummeri kasvaa, se '''luo kuorensa'''.''
#:: As it grows, a lobster will '''exuviate'''.

